  "notes": "Belgian vocal trance / trance-pop. `confidence` is low because the research rates the entry medium-low and says all parameters come from the trance convention page — a mark this model repeats. The three claims it does make are all encoded. \"Kick on every downbeat with the kick de-emphasised, regular open hi-hat on the upbeat\" gives the quietest accent tier of the three trance-pop models here and an open hat that is effectively unconditional. \"Long snare rolls building in velocity into the drop\" is the widest ramp in this section, 30-127, with a jitter of 4 so the climb reads as a single unbroken gesture. And the arrangement is the canonical trance form the entry spells out — \"DJ intro, build, mid-song climax then a beatless breakdown leaving melody/atmospherics alone for an extended stretch, then a gradual rebuild to a second drop\" — which is a 32-bar bridge and the highest drop-out probability in this section. The melody is \"a long sustained saw-lead anthem melody over an 8- or 16-bar loop, with a female topline doubling it\". ⚠ Every velocity, density and probability above is INFERRED.",
